h2. Database Schema Changes

*Note*: This feature primarily uses existing tables. New lead data will be stored in {{ide-phoenix}} database.

*New Table*: {{platinum_leads}} (in ide-phoenix)

{code:sql}
CREATE TABLE platinum_leads (
  id BIGINT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
  name VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
  company VARCHAR(255),
  email VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
  phone VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,
  message TEXT,
  source VARCHAR(50) DEFAULT 'platinum_hub',
  status VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'new',
  assigned_to BIGINT,
  created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  updated_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  INDEX idx_email (email),
  INDEX idx_status (status),
  INDEX idx_created_at (created_at)
) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
{code}

*Migration Strategy*:
* Deploy as zero-downtime migration
* Add indexes after table creation for large datasets
* Use {{pt-online-schema-change}} for production

