h2. Background Jobs

*Note*: Lead submission is synchronous, but email notifications use background jobs.

{code:typescript}
// Implement using Next.js API routes with queue (BullMQ or similar)
// Or delegate to ide-phoenix Sidekiq jobs

// ide-phoenix side (Ruby):
class SendLeadNotificationJob < ApplicationJob
  queue_as :default

  def perform(lead_id)
    lead = PlatinumLead.find(lead_id)
    LeadMailer.confirmation_email(lead).deliver_later
    AdminMailer.new_lead_notification(lead).deliver_later
  end
end
{code}

h2. Performance Optimization

*Caching Strategy*:
* Product data: Cache for 5 minutes (Redis or Next.js cache)
* Static assets: CDN with 1 year cache
* API responses: Stale-while-revalidate pattern

*Code Splitting*:
* Lazy load LeadForm component
* Lazy load ProductGrid when scrolled into view
* Separate bundles for authenticated vs unauthenticated users

*Image Optimization*:
* Use Next.js Image component
* Responsive images with srcset
* WebP format with PNG fallback
* Lazy loading for below-fold images

*Query Optimization*:
{code:sql}
-- Add indexes for common queries
CREATE INDEX idx_product_status ON products(status, featured, display_order);
CREATE INDEX idx_lead_status_created ON platinum_leads(status, created_at DESC);
{code}

*Database Connection Pooling*:
* Use connection pooling for API routes
* Set max connections: 10 per instance
* Implement retry logic with exponential backoff

h2. Security Considerations

*Authentication*:
* Use Auth0 JWT tokens
* Validate tokens on every protected route
* Implement token refresh logic
* Store tokens in httpOnly cookies

*Authorization*:
{code:typescript}
// lib/auth/permissions.ts
export const canAccessPlatinumBusiness = (user: User | null): boolean => {
  return user !== null && user.emailVerified;
};

export const canAccessAdminPanel = (user: User | null): boolean => {
  return user?.role === 'admin';
};
{code}

*Data Protection*:
* Encrypt sensitive data at rest
* Use HTTPS for all communications
* Implement rate limiting on API endpoints
* Sanitize all user inputs

*Input Validation*:
{code:typescript}
// lib/utils/validation.ts
import { z } from 'zod';

export const leadFormSchema = z.object({
  name: z.string().min(2, 'Name must be at least 2 characters').max(255),
  company: z.string().max(255).optional(),
  email: z.string().email('Invalid email address'),
  phone: z.string().regex(/^(\+62|62|0)[0-9]{9,12}$/, 'Invalid Indonesian phone number'),
  message: z.string().max(1000, 'Message too long').optional()
});

export type LeadFormData = z.infer<typeof leadFormSchema>;
{code}

*CSRF Protection*:
* Use Next.js built-in CSRF protection
* Validate origin header
* Implement double-submit cookie pattern

*XSS Prevention*:
* Sanitize all user inputs with DOMPurify
* Use React's built-in XSS protection
* Set Content Security Policy headers

{code:typescript}
// next.config.js
const securityHeaders = [
  {
    key: 'X-DNS-Prefetch-Control',
    value: 'on'
  },
  {
    key: 'X-Frame-Options',
